+# Codex Harness Upstream Provenance Contract
+
+Status: PARTIAL/BLOCKED, human-confirmed 2026-08-23
+
+## Goal
+
+Bind the bundled Codex App Server runtime to one immutable open-source
+`openai/codex` source identity without adopting or vendoring `codex-rs` as the
+Volt application foundation.
+
+## Frozen Scope
+
+- Bind the production manifest and candidate evidence to the exact upstream
+  tag object, peeled commit, root/App Server/protocol Git trees, Cargo.lock,
+  LICENSE, NOTICE, checked-in JSON schema manifest, and runtime-compatible
+  canonical schema tree.
+- Add a fail-closed source-tree verifier that is independent of ChatGPT.app.
+- Snapshot the npm runtime tarball into a private stable file before archive
+  inspection and extraction.
+- Bind the new fields in the JavaScript checker and Rust agentd manifest
+  authority.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- No Codex runtime upgrade or activation change.
+- No `codex-rs` vendoring, fork, or source build in the Volt workspace.
+- No change to TypeScript Core, Zig surface, or agentd ownership boundaries.
+- No claim that the official npm binary is reproducibly built from the pinned
+  source. The relationship remains
+  `official-release-reference-not-reproducibly-built`.
+- No use of `main`, `latest`, or another floating upstream ref.
+
+## Pinned Upstream
+
+| Field | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Repository | `https://github.com/openai/codex` |
+| Ref | `refs/tags/rust-v0.146.0-alpha.3.1` |
+| Tag object | `1128ef2c0eec791d1c6aeff0ecbb9f3f89b0aab2` |
+| Tag verification | `unsigned` |
+| Commit | `ff75c5b939c477c49eb1bd5248da6dab71b109d1` |
+| Root tree | `556ecec1e52bfb0636d8341514e42a46c8b639de` |
+| App Server tree | `4607330553f2d168e82031ba3870ddde1f918cb1` |
+| App Server protocol tree | `d8e9f888b7e83ca1bf0ce4293dfe847fd26063ed` |
+
+The unsigned tag is descriptive metadata, not a signature root. Runtime trust
+continues to require the npm integrity, Apple signing identity, binary digest,
+generated schema digest, runtime tree digest, sandbox evidence, and immutable
+commit/tree records.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+1. Missing, unknown, floating, or forged upstream fields fail closed.
+2. Source ref/tree, license/notice, schema additions/removals, raw schema content,
+   canonical schema content, and source-to-runtime schema binding drift fail closed.
+3. Runtime staging does not reopen the caller-owned tarball after its private
+   stable snapshot has been created.
+4. Focused Node/shell and Rust tests pass with the current diff inspected.
+5. Independent architecture and security reviewers report no blocker inside
+   this frozen scope.
+
+## Risk And Orchestration
+
+- Risk: high, because this changes runtime provenance and the manifest read
+  boundary.
+- Orchestration: panel; the current Codex session is the sole writer, with
+  independent read-only architecture and security reviewers.
+- Rollback: restore manifest/evidence/checker/agentd/stager as one unit. Old
+  manifest shapes remain rejected rather than supported in parallel.
+
+## Current Result
+
+- The frozen source-provenance scope passes its source, candidate staging,
+  rollback, syntax, formatting, and focused Rust manifest gates.
+- Whole-product production readiness remains blocked by the existing
+  runtime-tree path race in `crates/agentd-core/src/codex_process.rs`: entries
+  are checked with path metadata and later reopened without `O_NOFOLLOW` or a
+  descriptor-backed traversal.
+- Fixing that execution-time runtime-tree boundary is a follow-up contract; it
+  is not silently added to this provenance-only scope.
