-# Publish built overlay bytes behind a stable symlink. Every published sibling
-# remains byte-immutable: replacement atomically renames a temporary symlink
-# over DEST and never exchanges or edits the old target directory. A process
-# that already resolved the old real path can therefore finish on identical
-# bytes, while new consumers resolve the fully populated new sibling.
-# A pre-symlink legacy directory is deliberately rejected rather than removed;
-# that one-time migration must be performed while no Native process is using
-# the generated overlay.
